import Polyfold
/-! Blind formalization of V19_12 (the text's §19.2, Theorem 19.2.2, p. 869 of the Springer 2021
book; 2017: Theorem 19.1).

Text: (1) `T` is a topology on `|S|`; (2) `|Ψ(V)|` is open for `V ⊂ O` open; (3)
`|Ψ| : G\O → |S|` is a homeomorphism onto an open neighbourhood of `|α|`; (4) every point has a
countable neighbourhood basis; (5) every point has a metrizable open neighbourhood.

Choices:
- Setting: universe `0`: a groupoidal category `C : GroupoidalCategory.{0}` (the text's `S`) with
  a basic construction `B = (F, 𝓕)` (`C.BasicConstruction`, Definition 19.1.7, from the
  vocabulary).
- Hypothesis added: `B.U.HasClassUniformizers` (every class `z ∈ |S|` contains an object `α`
  with `F(α) ≠ ∅`).  Without it `|S|` itself is not in `T`, so (1) cannot hold; I read the text
  as presupposing it (the weakest of the vocabulary's two readings; `HasUniformizers` would be
  stronger).
- `T` (Definition 19.2.1) is written out here as `natOpen`: `W ⊂ |S|` is in `T` iff every `z ∈ W`
  has an object `α` with `|α| = z`, a `Ψ ∈ F(α)`, a point `ō` with `Ψ(ō) = α` and an open
  `V ∋ ō` with `|Ψ(V)| ⊂ W` (the existential reading, which is the vocabulary's `NatOpen`; I did
  not use the project's `natTop`).
- (1) is encoded as: the topology generated by `T` has exactly the members of `T` as open sets
  (equivalent to `T` being closed under finite intersections and arbitrary unions and containing
  `|S|`).  (2)–(5) are stated for that topology `τ`.
- (2), (3) are for every object `α` and every `Ψ ∈ F(α)` (`Ψ : G ⋉ O → S`, `O` with the
  topology of its M-polyfold structure).  `|Ψ(V)|` is the image of `V` under `q ↦ |Ψ(q)|`.
- (3): `G\O` = Mathlib's `MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient G O` with the quotient topology; the map
  `|Ψ|` is the one induced by `q ↦ |Ψ(q)|`; "homeomorphism onto an open neighbourhood of `|α|`"
  = `IsOpenEmbedding` with `|α|` in the range.
- (4) = `FirstCountableTopology`; (5): every `z` lies in a `τ`-open `W` which is metrizable in
  the subspace topology.
- Nothing looks doubtful to me.
-/
namespace RoundTrip.V19_12
open Polyfold

/-- The collection `T` of Definition 19.2.1. -/
def natOpen {C : GroupoidalCategory.{0}} (U : C.UniformizerConstruction)
    (W : Set C.OrbitSpace) : Prop :=
  ∀ z ∈ W, ∃ α : C.Obj, C.π α = z ∧ ∃ Ψ ∈ U.F α, ∃ o : Ψ.O, Ψ.obj o = α ∧
    ∃ V : Set Ψ.O, IsOpen V ∧ o ∈ V ∧ (fun q => C.π (Ψ.obj q)) '' V ⊆ W

/-- Theorem 19.2.2: the natural topology of a basic construction. -/
def B : Prop :=
  ∀ (C : GroupoidalCategory.{0}) (B : C.BasicConstruction), B.U.HasClassUniformizers →
    letI : TopologicalSpace C.OrbitSpace :=
      TopologicalSpace.generateFrom {W | natOpen B.U W}
    -- (1) `T` is a topology
    (∀ W : Set C.OrbitSpace, IsOpen W ↔ natOpen B.U W) ∧
    -- (2) `|Ψ(V)|` is open
    (∀ (α : C.Obj), ∀ Ψ ∈ B.U.F α, ∀ V : Set Ψ.O, IsOpen V →
      IsOpen ((fun q => C.π (Ψ.obj q)) '' V)) ∧
    -- (3) `|Ψ| : G\O → |S|` is a homeomorphism onto an open neighbourhood of `|α|`
    (∀ (α : C.Obj), ∀ Ψ ∈ B.U.F α,
      ∃ e : MulAction.orbitRel.Quotient Ψ.G Ψ.O → C.OrbitSpace,
        (∀ q : Ψ.O, e (Quotient.mk _ q) = C.π (Ψ.obj q)) ∧
        Topology.IsOpenEmbedding e ∧ C.π α ∈ Set.range e) ∧
    -- (4) first countable
    FirstCountableTopology C.OrbitSpace ∧
    -- (5) locally metrizable
    (∀ z : C.OrbitSpace, ∃ W : Set C.OrbitSpace, IsOpen W ∧ z ∈ W ∧
      TopologicalSpace.MetrizableSpace W)

end RoundTrip.V19_12
